    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag, following the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern throughout the stack:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean property to the Owner schema (so `OwnerDto` is generated with the field), documenting the 40\u201349 range approaching the limit of 50.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Schema SQL** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column so the flag persists and survives the re-fetch on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n4. **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 in `createOwner`, set the flag via a new `approachingCityCapacity(owner)` helper: `count >= 40 && count < 50`. It runs after `rejectWhenCityAtCapacity` (the unchanged hard rejection at `CITY_CAPACITY = 50`), evaluated on the pre-persist owner set like the sibling rules.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` mapping and a `capacityWarning(owner)` method treating a `null` stored value as `false`, so the field is always present in responses.\n\nThe provided acceptance test (`coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity`) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The hard rejection at 50 owners is unchanged.\n\nNote: this repo is not a git repository, so I made no commit \u2014 let me know if you'd like me to initialize one or if commits are handled elsewhere.",
